implement/references/ui-build/page-craft.md adapts rules from three sources.
All text is paraphrased, merged and reorganised; none is copied verbatim.

1. taste-skill by Leon Lin (MIT)
   Upstream-Repo: https://github.com/Leonxlnx/taste-skill
   Upstream-Path: skills/taste-skill (commits 3c7017d to 9b7d575)
   Used: page composition, contrast, motion safety, content honesty, theme
   lock and dark-mode rules; later also icon-family, italic-descender,
   glass-fallback, motivated-motion and animation-engine rules, and the
   redesign preservation list in ui-build.md ("Redesigns").

2. landing-page-design by Elaya (MIT)
   Upstream-Repo: https://github.com/elayadesign/ai-design-skills
   Upstream-Path: skills/landing-page-design
   Upstream-Commit: ded7efc
   Used: nested-radius formula, text wrapping, dead-link rule and the launch
   checklist.

3. impeccable by Paul Bakaus (Apache License 2.0)
   Upstream-Repo: https://github.com/pbakaus/impeccable
   Version: 4.1.1 (skill build), upstream HEAD 02523ae at adaptation
   Used: browser-surface theming, coloured-surface contrast, elevation and
   real-illustration rules from reference/craft-floor.md.
   Changes: rules paraphrased, merged with the sources above, and
   reorganised into page-craft.md sections. Licensed under the Apache
   License, Version 2.0; the full text is in LICENSE-APACHE-2.0.txt.


implement/references/ui-build/motion.md, the additions to
ui-build/usability.md (waiting states, toast or notification, long section
lists, nested menus, overlays) and the polish-pass testing line in
ui-build.md: rules rewritten in our own words from these sources. No text or
code is copied; links and read dates are in
explore-design/references/sources.md.

- Kubai087's "999 tips" posts on X (tips 001, 002, 005, 006, 008, 009, 011,
  014, 015, 016, 017 and the continuity post). Post text and attached
  prompts are not reproduced.
- Emil Kowalski's polish prompt (post on X) and his skills
  (https://github.com/emilkowalski/skills, MIT). The skills are installed
  separately and only named in motion.md's skill map; none is
  redistributed here.
- amicro by Subhan (https://github.com/Subhan-code/Amicro--Micro-transitions-,
  MIT): studied for the micro-transition shortlist; nothing copied.
- Kubai087's five anti-slop rules (post on X): the usability.md rules
  "Choose components by meaning" and "Cut copy that does no work". Post text
  is not reproduced.

